# W-B-F4. L §4.4 and §5.18: windows each splits a line by the windows it meets, and a line that meets none prints once;
# nothing may crash. has_car binds over cars over pm (a span the cut reads); q2 states windows each and meets no window,
# so it prints as q1 does. snap10 crashed (REFCORE-NOT-YET … TypeError: WCut.__new__() takes 3 positional arguments
# but 4 were given: the windows-each cut plus one day).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

source s "s"

kind cars

input pm: month

def has_car: bool = any(true for c in cars over pm)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  cars + [c1] lives 2026-01-01..
  pm = 2026-03

ask q1: has_car law 2026-06-30 as known 2026-06-30
ask q2: has_car law 2026-06-30 as known 2026-06-30 windows each
=== expect
q1: true
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
q2: true
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
